WHAT TO DO WHEN A UNIT/FLAT IS TRANSFERED ?

SIMPLE METHOD
-------------
1. Master Maint.
3. Member Details

   1. Edit Names, Area, Unit, Open Bal ? 
      say Y - for Yes
      
      Simply change the Old Member's Name and type the New Member's name
      
      
RIGHT METHOD
------------      
1. Master Maint. (from MAIN MENU)
   1. Create Account > Enter the New Member's Name > Select GROUP Member's Dues
   
NEXT .....
1. Master Maint. (from MAIN MENU)
3. Member Details > 


      ฺฤฤฤฤฤฤฤ B i l l     O p t i o n s ฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฟ
      ณ 1. Edit Name, Area, Unit, Open. Bal ?   ณ 
      ณ 2. Allow editing of Rates ?             ณ 
      ณ 3. Sort according to Flat Nos. ?        ณ 


   STEPS TO FOLLOW :
   (As show in Menu above)
   (It is recommended to Take a Backup before doing this process)
   
   Say  Yes to Option No. 1. Enter the Unit/Flat No, Area..
   Next Yes to Option No. 3. to Sort the Flat Nos
   Next Yes to Option No. 2. to Enter the Rates of New Member
   Next Yes to Option No. 1. to Enter "X" in CAT (category) column.
                             against the Old member.
                             marking "X" will not generate subsequent bills for old member.
   Also following this method will created two different ledgers for both old and new members.

----------------------------------------------------------------
HOW DO I SAVE-GUARD THE DATA ?
   Take a Regular Back-up of your Data
   on Floppies, CDs, Harddisks or other Media
   
7. Accessories
5. Back/Res. Data

   Your Floppies may get corrupted or your harddisks might crash
   to secure your data, take regular backup of your data
   on Floppies and Harddisks, Burning CDs with your data is a 
   prefered option, have your data backed up on atleast 2 media.
   
   A compressed file is created while taking a backup with the 
   extension .arj
   
   You may even copy or burn into a CD, the whole c:\pace directory
   depending on the Drive the package is installed.
   
   If your data looks haywire, don't take a backup, 
   you might overwrite and damage the existing backed-up data
   Contact Databyte  Computers instead.
   
   Unless absolutely sure, Don't restore your data.  
   Or do so at a different location.

   ALSO SET PASSWORDS TO ENTER THE PACKAGE
   if you Computer is Accessible by Un-authorised Persons.

----------------------------------------------------------------
CAN I GENERATE SEPARATE BILLS, WITH A DIFFERENT BILLING STRUTURE,
DIFFERENT RATE, APART FROM THE REGULAR BILLS ?

YES, FOLLOW STEPS TO DO SO.

STEP 1 - Take a backup
---------------------
It is recommended to take a Backup of your Data, incase you want to 
revert back your actions.

STEP 2 - Store current Rate in a Library
----------------------------------------
Next Store your current Billing Rates, in a Library, through the
Library Options.

3. Bills/Vouchers 
5. Library Option

       Library Options
       --------------- 
1. List Library Names ?       No
2. Clear all Current Rates ?  No
3. Load Library ?             No
4. Delete Library ?           No
5. Store Current Rates ?      Yes - give a meaningful Name
                                 e.g. April - for April Rates
                                   or Regular - for Regular Rates
                                   
Whatever Name you enter, you can revert back to the Master Rates
by using the Load Library Option, and selecting the specified Library Name.
You may create as many Libraries you want.                                    

STEP 3 - Clear Current Rates
----------------------------
Next use the Library Option to clear the current rates
2. Clear all Current Rates ?  Yes


STEP 4. - Create a Ledger Account
---------------------------------
e.g you want to create an item call - Major Repair Charges
according Create a Ledger Account

1. Master Maint.
1. Create Account

STEP 5 - Create a New Bill Structure
------------------------------------
Refer to above < DESIGNING THE BILL STRUCTURE >

except When prompted for Bill Structure Date :
give a new Bill Structure Date 

STEP 6. - Enter the Rates for the new Item created
--------------------------------------------------
1. Master Maint.
3. Member Details

   1. Edit Names, Area, Unit, Open Bal ? 
      say N - for No    
      
   2. Allow Editing of Rates ?           
      say Y - for Yes     

Enter the rates in the new column

You may save the New Rates again in a Library for future use.
by making use of Store Current Rates, via Library Options

Proceed further to Generate the Bills.
Select the same Bill Structure Date and not the Regular Bill Structure Date.

Next you may revert back to your Regular Billing Rates, by
using the Libray Option, Load Library.
   
----------------------------------------------------------------
LIST OF NEW FEATURES ADDED, SINCE THE LAST MANUAL PRINTED..
----------------------------------------------------------------
1.  Use <Ctrl+T> to copy Title of a Member e.g. Mr.,Mrs. Dr.,Capt, etc
    instead of <Ctrl+A> used earlier.

2.  While Editing Rates, use the <spacebar> to Display Names and Unit Nos.
    when your Left part of the screen does not display the names, unit nos,
    while Nagivating on the Right side of the Screen.

3.  AlphaNumeric Unit Nos can be used, unlike earlier only Numeric.

4.  Cost Centres - You can now bifurcate expenses etc. building wise or 
    Create your own Cost Centres

5.  Option to print Non Billing Receipts
    e.g. Receipts can be printed, which are directly credited to
         Transfer Fees, Admission Fees, Sale of Scrap etc.       

6.  Option to Print in 2 Column format
    e.g. 6 items on the Left and 6 items on the right of the bill
         in 6 inch paper.

7.  Option to Print Receipt below a bill

8.  Option to Print the Ledger below a bill

9.  Option to Print Due Date, Rateable Value in the bill.

10. Option for 16 items in tbe bill, instead of 12 items earlier
    which has to be enabled in the Setup Option - Advanced Settings

11. Receipts and Payment Statement

12. Additional Categories apart from S - for Shop , G - for Garage 
    now can have F - for Flat, L - for Gala, O - for Office
                 P - for Parking # , U - for Unit No 

13. Option to copy similar wing, by pressing <Ctrl+W> thru member details 

14. Option to copy similar Area, by pressing <Ctrl+R> thru member details 

15. Option to copy similar Bldg, by pressing <Ctrl+B> thru member details 

16. Rebate Options
    You can now have an Option for Rebates, enabling it thru Setup, and
    Advanced Settings, and setting the rates thru Rebates Options

17. Option to Store and Print on Bills Rateable Value    

18. Option to Sort Receipts List Datewise, Receipt Nowise or Unitwise

19. In Ledger Use F1 Key to Group Select, now also use F3 Key to De-select 
    a whole Group of Ledger Accounts, Use F2 to Tick all.

20. In Ledger Use F4 Key to Select all Accounts with Debit Balances.    
              Use F5 Key to Select all Accounts with Credit Balances.    
              Use F2 Key to Select all Accounts or De-Select all accounts

21. Option to Modify Interest (only in Special Version)

22. Option not to Charge Interest on a Particular Amount in Bill.

23. Option to Create and Feed similar Bill Rates, quickly on a press of 
    of Key. viz. Press <f1> Key to replace similar values for first field
    in Bill etc.
    Press <Ctrl+A> to Calculate Rates - Areawise and replace immediately.            
    Option to Feed Rates in Master based on a set pattern.              
    via     1. Master Maint.  --  3. Members Details
    
24. Option to Display and Print Principal and Accumulated Interest
    in Bill Register, if Opted for Simple Interest.
    via     4. Accounts Books --  4. Bill Register
    
25. Option to Display and Print Expense and Receipts Summary
    via     5. Reports        --  7. Expense Summary.     

26. Option to Delete all Transactions, within a selected Date Range
    Use Cautiously ....
    can be Deleted on entering of Valid Deletion Password only.
    
    via     3. Bills/Vouchers --  2. Daybook/Erase

27. Option to Replace the Word <Interest> with your own word. 
    e.g. use the word <Penalty> instead of <Interest>
    
    Option to Replace the Term <Bldg> with your own Term.
    e.g. Floor, Site or Level etc.
    
    Option to Replace the Term <Interest on Arrears> 
    with your own Term.
    
    via     8. Setup        --  7. Advance Settings

28. Option to have more lines for footnote, now can be 
    extended to 18 lines.    
    
    via     8. Setup        --  7. Advance Settings
                  
29. Option to Toggle X
    Entering "X" in the cat (category) column, through Member Details
    will prevent generating bills for those members
    
    Suppose you need to generate a set of bills for some members
    and avoid some. Enter "X" in the cat (category) column, against 
    the menbers whom you don't want to generate bills,
    Next Generate the Bills ..... all bills pertaining to 
    members who are not marked "X" bill be billed.
    
    Next Press Ctrl+X to toggle the X marked members
    Generate the next set of bills (with a different date)
    
    This feature will bypass any cat with an "S" , "G" or any other category

30. Reminder Letter    

31. Payment List
    sorted Datewise or Document Nowise or Accountwise
    with Option for Narration 
    
32. Earlier payments received a day before the date of the bill were
    considered, payments made on the day of the bill date were not taken
    into account.
    Now payments recorded even on the Bill date are considered.
    e.g. if Bill date is 01.01.2005 and payment is recorded on the same day
         credit is given to the party.

33. Option for Mini Receipt with Bill.

34. Option for Bankwise Receipt List

35. Option for Daywise Interest Calculation

36. Option to Multiply the existing Rates with any Amount
    by Pressing Ctrl + m
    Similar to Pressing Ctrl + a - for Areawise Calculation 

37. Option to Divide the existing Rates with any Amount              
    by Pressing Ctrl + d
38. Collection Register - under Account Books
39. Option for Individual Bill FootNote.   
40. Signature Register (acknowledgement for any document)
41. Refresh Opening Balance will exclude Member's Opening Balance
42. Changes in Default Password setup to avoids inserting error passwords. (v 5.90)
43. Shows Groups in Opening / Closing Balance Lists & option for Nil amounts (v 5.91)
44. Option to pick up Pre-defined Narrations in 3 & 4th lines too.
45. Option in Recepts List for Non Member-related receipts (v 5.92)
46. Option for Replication of Members, to create another set of billing
    e.g. Major Repairs,  with separate ledger accounts.
    can also set separate interest rates to this set of accounts (v 5.97)
47. Option for Mini Receipt in Bills, including 2 columnar bills.(v 6.00)    
48. Press Ctrl+S to Search on Unit No.
    Press Ctrl+F to Find Member's Name while entering Receipts etc.
49. Additional Field - X instead on CATegory field to input X and N.    
50. Oustanding List with Ageing Option (3-3-7) (v 6.04)
51. Library Option - Option to pickup Rates from Registers    
------------------------------------------------------------------------

(f) While entering vouchers relating to Cash Withdrawal from, Enter the Same through
    Bank Payments ONCE only, and NOT again in the Cash Receipts. Cash on hand is 
    automatically adjusted.  The same applies for Cash Deposits made in Bank.
    
    If Cash is received only from other sources, and not through Banks, then
    enter a voucher through Cash Receipts.


Advance Options (under Setup)

 1)  The CODE CONVERTOR is used to shuffle any Ledger Account, and place it at a different Location.

     e.g. Computer Sytems which is a FIXED ASSET is grouped under INVESTMENT by mistake,
          can be corrected by changing the code to a FIXED ASSETS code.
          (all transactions pertaining to the same will also be rectified automaticaly)
  
 2)  The GROUP CONVERTOR can likewise be used to change a whole Group into
     another Group. 

     e.g. Convert all FIXED ASSETS Group to DEPOSITS Group
           (the above two tools are to used cautiously)

 4)  MERGE ACCOUNT : This tool is used to Merge two Ledger Accounts
     e.g. Wages a/c and Salary a/c is to be merged to form only a single
          account (viz. Salary account) at the end of the year
          
          
 5) DELETE MEMO ENTRIES : Memo Entries are Temporary Journal Entries
    entered anytime during the year for generating I & E a/c, Balance Sheet
    etc.  These entries can be deleted at once using this Option.

    
                 G E N E R A L     T I P S  


(a) The Main Menu Consists of 8 Options apart from Quit.

(b) You may Move the Highlighted Bar or Enter the Option Number.

(c) When the Options are selected a Sub-Menu shall appear on the Sides.

(d) When the Sub-Menus are selected a further Menu might appear.

(e) You are always guided through the Package by way of a Dialog Box, Messages
    You have to Select the Option desired by you

    Normally the Standard Option is selected and you simply have to Press ENTER.
    
(f) You are advised to regularly BACKUP Your DATA.


 ษอออออออออออออออออป  
 บ STEPS TO FOLLOW บ    MAIN MENU  ออ Select ACCESSORIES ออ Select BACKUP     
 ศอออออออออออออออออผ 
           
    It is recommended to maintain Two Sets of Floppies for Backup.
    
    Mark Floppies as Set A and Set B, and Alternately use each floppy
    for Backing up.
    
    For Multiple Societies Write the Name of Society on each Floppy,
    and Select the respective Floppies as Backup.

    Enter a meaningful Backup file name, in place of XFILE (default name)  
    the system will remember the last mentioned file name. Different societies
    should have a different Backup File Name, never use similar file names.

    

                          P R I N T I N G   


(a) Before attempting to Print a Report, do check that the Printer is Online.

(b) All Reports can be printed on the 80, 132 or 136 Column Printer.

(c) Most of the Reports require only the 80 Column Printer,
    Unless the Printer Size is Asked?
    
(d) When the Printer Size is asked, and You are using the 80 Column Printer,
    Reports are printed in the Condensed Form.
    
(e) Almost all the Reports that can be viewed on the Screen, can be printed.

              
